UID:42950@google.com
CREATED:20260507T052712Z
DESCRIPTION:Come one\, come all! Join us on Zoom for a reading series open 
 to beginning leftists\, veteran activists\, and the socialism-curious alike
 . Texts include "The ABCs of Socialism" by writers at Jacobin Magazine\, "R
 eform or Revolution" by Rosa Luxemburg\, and "The Communist Manifesto" by K
 arl Marx. Be ready to learn and to question your presuppositions about soci
 alism!\nFirst up!\nIf you're not sure about socialism (or if you are sure b
 ut you need some talking points to clap back with) this is where you start.
  Learn the answers to questions like: "Socialism sounds good in theory\, bu
 t doesn’t human nature make it impossible to realize?" "Doesn’t socialism a
 lways end in dictatorship?" And even\, "Will socialists take my Kenny Loggi
 ns records?"Socialism doesn't have to be scary or boring. Come find out wha
 t it's really all about! \n\n\n\nRSVP: https://solidarity.socodsa.org/socod
 sa-101-book-club
LAST-MODIFIED:20260514T210449Z
LOCATION:https://zoom.us/meetings/92028858854/invitations?signature=Eqxlg0h
 MPPFA_CEAELyp6uJeIz-_H2on2ZAYPAxwd9U
SEQUENCE:4
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:📚 DSA 101.5 Book Club­­
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
