UID:33838@google.com
CREATED:20260511T050531Z
DESCRIPTION:My Mom taught me that “Passover should be an event that everyon
 e should experience at least once.” But didn’t just say those words but she
  lived by them\, She wrote and improved upon\, a family Haggadah\, a guide 
 book meant to help everyone\, even the leader keep track with the story and
  the teaching of what Passover is and why we celebrate it. She always made 
 adjustments to the seder to being as inclusive as possible with who was com
 ing\, so they could enjoy the evening\, and even made dietary adjustments f
 or those who desired it just so they wouldn’t have to be left out.  My fami
 ly has continued that tradition after her passing. But now I want to expand
  it. I want more than just my immediate friends and family to enjoy the Pas
 sover seder I want as many people that want to join in to enjoy it as well.
  So that is why I am hosting this seder this year and my hope is to do it e
 very year going forward.\n \nTime and Place:\n \nSunday April 19th\, 4 PM t
 o 7PM Redwood Forest Friends Meeting Quaker Hall\n1647 Guerneville Rd\, San
 ta Rosa\, CA 95403\n \nPlease RSVP if you are interested in coming as it he
 lps me understand how many table spots\, place settings\, food and drink ne
 eds to be accounted for.  I will also welcome any volunteers who would be f
 ree to help me out with hosting this event\, This includes setting the tabl
 e\, getting food prepared to be served for the dinner as well as for appeti
 zers\, cleaning up and lastly providing food via Potluck style.   You are w
 elcome to bring a potluck dish that can be served cold or warmed up in the 
 kitchen we have to use\, but sadly we will be unable to use the kitchen to 
 create new food\, so please have it prepped before coming. I would desire t
 hat dishes remain “Passover Kosher”\, which is a special kind of kosher jus
 t for Passover\, it basically means almost nothing with grain in it\, which
  can be a lot of things. If you want to confirm with me if your dish is Kos
 her or not\, please contact me directly and ill be happy to chat with you a
 bout it.\nThe Seder is split into two parts with a big feast of a dinner in
  between. Snacking and drinking beverages during the seder is encouraged as
  we know people can get hungry\, while waiting for the dinner.\n \nThe Sede
 r is interactive for all\, as we will all be reading from the Haggadah book
  (95% in English) with me as a guide and leader.  Dressing casual or fancy 
 and everything in between is welcome\, being comfortable and relaxing is a 
 core tenant of the holiday so we want everyone to feel like they can chill 
 with friends. Alcohol will be at the event but there is no requirement to d
 rink and non-alcoholic beverages will be available for all.\n \nIf you have
  any questions at all please reach out to me via my email Cochair.joel@soco
 dsa.org\nI hope to see you all there\, it should be a great evening.\n \n- 
 Joel Berger\n\nRSVP: https://solidarity.socodsa.org/soco-dsa-passover-seder
 -2026
LAST-MODIFIED:20260511T053224Z
LOCATION:1647 Guerneville Rd\, Santa Rosa\, CA 95403\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:SoCo DSA Passover Seder 2026
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
